The objects of the Corporation shall be - (a} to administer a deposit protection scheme for the member under this Order;

(b) to provide protection against the loss of part or all of the deposits of a member institution;

(c) to provide incentives for sound risk management in the financial and

(d) to promote or contribute to the stability of the financial system. of Corporation.

( 1) The Corporation may invest in

(a) any stocks, funds, shares or securities in companies incorporated or operating in Brunei Darussalam; and

(b) any investment in any entity or instrument of issuers based in any country or territory alternating or originating in any other currency,

(i) any obligation of a corporation, commercial bank or a bankcompany, asset-backed security and mortgage-backed • issued or unconditionally guaranteed by a corporate or trust; any repurchase and reverse repurchase with a major commercial bank or a primary dealer;

(ii) futures, forwards, options contracts or swaps on any which are traded on an exchange;

(iii) any security listed and traded on an exchange;

(iv) any exchange-traded funds, instruments that provide to market indices for any investment, a private fund and a hedge fund;

(v) any Islamic financial instrument;

(vi) any bullion, commodity and currency;

(vii) any other specific investment not included in this subsection as may be approved by the Corporation.

(2) Any investment from the fund shall be in accordance with Hukum year.

In this Part - means the unpaid balance of the aggregate of deposits as defined in received or held by a member institution from or on behalf of a in the usual course of the business of deposit-taking of the member and shall include -

(a) on-member institution Brunei dollar and foreign currency deposits;

(b) a bank draft, certified cheque or other similar instrument or instruction, drawn or made against a deposit account for which the institution is primarily liable;

(c) a cheque entered into a payment system or a clearing house notwithstanding any delay or failure by the member institution in crediting the account; or

(d) any other liability or financial instrument as may be specified by the Corporation, but excludes -

(i) a deposit that is not payable in Brunei Darussalam;

(ii) money market deposits;

(iii) any structured deposits;

(iv) negotiable instruments of deposit and other bearer deposits;

(v) agreements; and

(vi) any other liability or financial instrument as may be specified by the Corporation; "trust accounts" includes monies held on account for the purpose of trust.

